      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    # Load data without modifying it\n    data = np.load(\"vectors_secondary.npy\", mmap_mode=\"r\")\n    n, d = data.shape\n\n    # Work in float64 for numerically stable, exact-as-possible distance computation.\n    # Convert once; 8000x1024 float64 is only ~64MB, easily fits in memory.\n    X = np.array(data, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    # Precompute squared norms of each row.\n    norms = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', X, X)\n\n    total = 0.0\n    block_size = 1000  # tune for memory/time balance: block_size * n * 8 bytes per block\n\n    Xt = X.T  # reuse transposed view for matmul\n\n    for start in range(0, n, block_size):\n        end = min(start + block_size, n)\n        block = X[start:end]                     # (b, d)\n        # Dot products between block rows and all rows via BLAS (fast).\n        dot = block @ Xt                          # (b, n)\n        # Squared Euclidean distances using ||a||^2 + ||b||^2 - 2 a.b\n        sq = norms[start:end, None] + norms[None, :] - 2.0 * dot\n        # Guard against tiny negative values due to floating point round-off.\n        np.maximum(sq, 0.0, out=sq)\n        dist = np.sqrt(sq)\n        total += float(dist.sum())\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total!r}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
